{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.wallawalla.edu/fileadmin/user_upload/Academic_Administration/Job_Postings/2026-06-23_Business_Management_job_posting.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty in Management/Marketing",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty in Management/Marketing.  \nJob Title \n \nFull-time Faculty in Business \nDepartment/School \n \nSchool of Business \nClassification \n \nExempt (Salary) \nCompensation and \nBenefits \nPlacement of  the new hire within the salary pay grade is dependent on qualifications and \nprofessional teaching experience. The pay grade assigned to this position ranges from $67,067 \n– $86,279 annually. \nBenefits: May include medical, retirement, paid time off, and more. To learn more, visit: \nwallawalla.edu/benefits. \n \nAvailable \n \nJanuary 1, 2027 \nDescription: \n \n \nThe School of Business invites applications for a full-time faculty position in business to begin as \nsoon as January 1, 2027.  Core teaching responsibilities are in management and marketing but \ncandidates with a range of experience including in AI/information systems, business law, and \nentrepreneurship are also encouraged to apply. \n \nResponsibilities include: (a) teaching, academic advising, and mentoring students; (b) engaging in \nscholarly and professional activities; (c) serving on universities committees; (d) and \ndemonstrating commitment to community service.   \n \nQualifications: Preferred qualifications include: (1) earned doctorate in business/management area; (2) other \nnon-business doctorate, including juris doctorate, and an MBA degree or significant teaching and \nwork experience in the teaching area; (3) or an MBA or relevant master’s degree and significant \nteaching and work experience in the teaching area. Applicants must already have authorization to \nwork in the U.S. \n \nApplicants should be able to: (a) use technology effectively in teaching and learning; (b) bring \nreal-world experiences to the classroom; (c) work collaboratively; (d) show evidence of scholarly \nand professional activity; (e) demonstrate a commitment to Christian higher education and the \nintegration of faith and learning. \n \nApply: \n \nProspective candidates interested in the position are asked to complete an online faculty \nemployment application and attach a cover letter, CV, and statement of teaching philosophy. \nApplication materials due before September 1, 2026. Consideration of applicants will continue \nuntil the position is filled.  \n \nQuestions: For further information, please contact David Lennox by phone (509) 527-2051 or email \nDavid.Lennox@wallawalla.edu. To learn more about our program visit our website at \nhttp://business.wallawalla.edu. \n \n \n"
    },
    "https://www.wallawalla.edu/fileadmin/user_upload/Academic_Administration/Job_Postings/2026-09-02_MBA_Faculty_position.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty, MBA Program Director",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty, MBA Program Director.  \nJob Title Full-Time Faculty, MBA Program Director \n \nDepartment/School School of Business \n \nClassification Exempt (Salary) \n \nCompensation and \nBenefits \n \nPlacement of  the new hire within the salary pay grade is dependent on qualifications and professional \nteaching experience. The pay grade assigned to this position ranges from $67,068 – $86,280 annually. \n \nBenefits: May include medical, retirement, paid time off, and more. To learn more, visit: \nwallawalla.edu/benefits. \n \nAvailable \n \nSeptember 1, 2026 \nJob Description Walla Walla University’s School of Business invites applications for a full-time position as faculty and \ndirector of the MBA Program. The director reports to the dean of the School of Business and is \nresponsible for coordinating student support and success from application through degree completion; \nproviding leadership for MBA recruitment, outreach, and marketing, including developing relationships \nwith employers and other external partners; coordinating program administration; and working \ncollaboratively with School and University leadership on curriculum development, program assessment, \nand continuous improvement. As a member of the School faculty, the director will participate in School-\nwide activities, engage in scholarship and professional development, and teach primarily online graduate-\nlevel business courses. \n \nQualifications • An earned doctorate from an accredited program in business or a related field is preferred.  \nCandidates with a relevant master’s or other advanced degree and substantial professional leadership \nexperience will also be considered.  \n• Strong leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills and an ability to work effectively with \nstudents, faculty, university colleagues, employers, and other external partners. \n• Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching, preferably in online or graduate-level environments. \n• A commitment to ongoing scholarly engagement and professional growth. \n• Additional experience in one or more of the following areas is desirable: graduate or professional \nprogram administration; student, employee, or client support and success; student recruitment and \noutreach; employer and external relationship building; curriculum development and program \nassessment. \n \nApply Prospective candidates interested in the position are asked to submit an online faculty employment \napplication and attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and statement of teaching philosophy. \nConsideration of applicants will continue until the position is filled.  \n \nQuestions Contact Dr. Jonathan Duncan, Graduate Dean, at Jonathan.Duncan@wallawalla.edu or 509-527-2368. \nVisit the Walla Walla University School of Business website to learn more about the business program. \n \n \n"
    },
    "https://www.wallawalla.edu/fileadmin/user_upload/Academic_Administration/Job_Postings/2026-05-19_Psychology_faculty_job_posting.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty in Psychology",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty in Psychology.  \nJob Title Full-Time Faculty Position in Psychology \nDepartment/School School of Education & Psychology \nClassification Exempt (Salary) \nCompensation and \nBenefits \n \nPlacement of  the new hire within the salary pay grade is dependent on qualifications and \nprofessional teaching experience. The pay grade assigned to this position ranges from $68,342.03 –  \n$86,279.75 annually. \nBenefits: May include medical, retirement, paid time off, and more. To learn more, visit: \nwallawalla.edu/benefits. \nAvailable July 1, 2027 \nJob Description The School of Education and Psychology at Walla Walla University is seeking applications for a faculty \nposition in psychology. We seek an enthusiastic person whose primary instructional role includes \nteaching undergraduate psychology classes, as well as supporting student engagement in research and \nother professional development activities. \nThe ideal candidate will be committed to excellence in teaching, advising, and mentoring students. \nWhile teaching is primary, significant other responsibilities include academic advising and service on \nuniversity-wide committees.  The successful candidate will be a dedicated Seventh-day Adventist \nChristian committed to integrating their faith with teaching and scholarship, and should also bring real-\nworld experiences to the learning environment. Evidence should be provided of collaborative work, \nscholarly activity, and a commitment to Christian higher education. \nQualifications An earned doctorate in Psychology. A demonstrated commitment to Seventh-day Adventist education, \nto community service, and to research and writing for scholarly publications is expected. \nApply Prospective candidates interested in the position are asked to submit an online faculty employment \napplication and attach a cover letter, curricula vitae, and statement of teaching philosophy.  \nThree letters of recommendation are to be sent by the recommenders to Dr. Maria Bastien Valenca, \nDean, School of Education & Psychology to maria.bastien@wallawalla.edu. Consideration of \napplicants will continue until the position is filled. \nQuestions Contact Dr. Maria Bastien Valenca at maria.bastien@wallawalla.edu or 509-527-2370. To learn more \nabout the School of Education & Psychology visit our website at \nhttps://www.wallawalla.edu/academics/areas-of-study/education-and-psychology  \n \n"
    },
    "https://www.wallawalla.edu/fileadmin/user_upload/Academic_Administration/Job_Postings/2026-08-12_General_Nursing_Faculty_Job_Posting.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty in Nursing",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty in Nursing.   \nJob Title: Full-time Faculty Position in Nursing \nDepartment/School: School of Nursing  \nClassification: Exempt (Salary) \nCompensation and \nBenefits: \nCompensation: Placement of the new hire within the faculty pay schedule is dependent on \neducation, qualifications, certifications, and professional experience. Salary range: $68,983 to \n$92,370 annually, with additional nursing program stipend up to $10,000 for the 2026/2027 \nacademic year.  \nBenefits: May include medical, retirement, paid time off, and more. To learn more, visit: \nhttps://www.wallawalla.edu/human-resources/employee-resources/benefits-perks  \nAvailable: September 1, 2026 \nDescription: \n \nWalla Walla University’s School of Nursing seeks a dedicated and experienced nursing \nprofessional to join our faculty as a full-time faculty member. This role is central to delivering \nhigh-quality undergraduate nursing education through classroom, clinical, laboratory, and \nsimulation instruction. We are looking for an enthusiastic educator who is committed to student \nsuccess, mentorship, and professional excellence. The faculty member will be actively involved in \ncurriculum development, program evaluation, and continuous improvement of teaching and \nlearning strategies. This position offers the opportunity to model professional nursing practice \nand contribute to the growth and development of future nurses. The successful candidate will be \na dedicated Christian who integrates faith with teaching and scholarship, and who actively \nsupports the mission of Walla Walla University and the values of the Seventh-day Adventist \ntradition. \n \nResponsibilities: \n \n Teach assigned didactic, clinical, simulation, or lab courses in the undergraduate program.  \n Supervise students in clinical settings, promoting safe, ethical, and competent nursing care. \n Collaborate with community agencies to establish and maintain clinical partnerships. \n Advise and mentor students, fostering professional growth. \n Participate in course development, curriculum review and program evaluation activities. \n Participate in School of Nursing and institutional committees, meetings, and other activities. \n Collaborate with colleagues to foster a positive learning environment and address diverse learning \nneeds. \n \n  \n\nQualifications: \n \nEducation: \n• Master’s degree in nursing (MSN) required \n• Doctorate in Nursing or related field (DNP, PhD, EdD), preferred \n \n \nExperience:  \n• Clinical expertise and experience relevant to assigned teaching areas \n \nLicensure:  \n• Current, unencumbered RN license in WA and OR (or be eligible for) \nPreferred Qualifications:  \n• Experience teaching in classroom, clinical, or simulation settings \n• Clinical or teaching experience in adult medical-surgical nursing or complex acute care \nnursing. Relevant experience may include medical-surgical, intensive care, \nprogressive/step-down, emergency, or other high-acuity clinical settings \n \nSkills and Abilities: \n• Strong commitment to teaching excellence and student-centered learning \n• Strong communication and interpersonal skills \n• Ability to work effectively as part of a collaborative academic team \n• Ability to work effectively with students of diverse backgrounds and learning styles \n• Capacity to work with students one-on-one and in small groups to support individualized \nlearning \n• Highly organized and adaptable, with the flexibility to respond to changes within the \nhealth care and academic system \n• Must have a valid driver’s license, reliable transportation, and the ability to travel for \nstudent visits \n \nApply: Qualified candidates interested in the position are asked to submit an online faculty application \nand attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and statement of teaching philosophy.  Consideration \nof applicants will continue until the position is filled. \nQuestions: Kari Firestone, School of Nursing Dean, at 509-527-2145 or kari.firestone@wallawalla.edu. To \nlearn more about our program visit our website at:  \nhttps://www.wallawalla.edu/academics/areas-of-study/nursing/ \n \n "
    },
    "https://www.wallawalla.edu/fileadmin/user_upload/Academic_Administration/Job_Postings/2025-07-28_Adjunct_Nursing_Faculty_Job_Posting.pdf": {
      "title": "Adjunct Nursing Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Nursing Faculty.   \nJob Title: Adjunct Faculty Position in Nursing \n \nDepartment/School: School of Nursing, Portland, Oregon Campus  \n \nClassification: Contract Employee \n \nCompensation and \nBenefits: \nThe compensation for adjunct faculty positions in the School of Nursing is based on a per-\ncredit rate for didactic instruction. The rate of pay is determined by the type of teaching \nassignment, faculty qualifications, and experience, as well as the specific needs of the course(s) \n(e.g., hours and responsibilities) being taught. The per-credit rate ($855-995) is determined by \nthe department and will be outlined in the individual adjunct faculty contract prior to the start \nof the appointment. No benefits apply for this position.  \n \nAvailable: Ongoing \n \nDescription: \n \nWalla Walla University’s School of Nursing seeks a dedicated and experienced nursing \nprofessional to join our faculty as an adjunct faculty member. This role will involve teaching, \nmentoring, and preparing nursing students to excel as nursing professionals. We are looking \nfor an enthusiastic educator with a commitment to student success. This position will \ncollaborate closely with faculty colleagues to deliver high quality, evidence-based education in \nthe classroom. The successful candidate will be a dedicated Christian committed to integrating \ntheir faith with teaching and scholarship. \n \nResponsibilities: \n \n• Teach assigned nursing theory or didactic courses in accordance with established syllabi \nand course outcomes. \n• Prepare and deliver engaging, evidence-based instruction through in-person or online \nmodalities as assigned. \n• Use varied teaching methods to support diverse learners and foster active student \nengagement. \n• Assess student learning through quizzes, exams, assignments, and participation, and \nprovide timely, constructive feedback. \n• Maintain accurate course records, grades, and documentation in the university’s learning \nmanagement system. \n• Communicate regularly with students regarding course expectations, performance, and \nsupport resources. \n \n \n  \n\nQualifications: \n \nEducation: \n• Master’s degree in nursing (MSN) required.  \n• Doctorate in Nursing or related field (DNP, PhD, EdD), preferred. \n \nExperience: \n• Clinical expertise and experience relevant to assigned teaching areas. \n \nLicensure: \n• Current, unencumbered RN license in OR and WA (or be eligible for). \n \nPreferred Qualifications: \n• Experience teaching in classroom, clinical, or simulation settings. \n• Clinical or teaching experience in maternal newborn (OB, pediatric, or community/public \nhealth nursing. \n \nSkills and Abilities: \n• Strong commitment to teaching excellence and student-centered learning. \n• Strong communication and interpersonal skills. \n• Ability to work effectively as part of a collaborative academic team. \n• Ability to work effectively with students of diverse backgrounds and learning styles. \n• Capacity to work with students one-on-one and in small groups to support individualized \nlearning. \n• Highly organized and adaptable, with the flexibility to respond to changes within the \nhealth care and academic system. \n \nApply: Qualified candidates interested in the position are asked to submit an online faculty \napplication and attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and statement of teaching philosophy. \n \nQuestions: Kari Firestone, School of Nursing Dean, at 509-527-2145 or kari.firestone@wallawalla.edu. \nTo learn more about our program visit our website at:  \nhttps://www.wallawalla.edu/academics/areas-of-study/nursing/ \n \n "
    },
    "https://www.wallawalla.edu/fileadmin/user_upload/Academic_Administration/Job_Postings/2026-08-04_Social_Work_faculty_position_CP.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty in Social Work",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty in Social Work.  \nJob Title: Full-Time Faculty Position, Social Work Programs \nDepartment/School: School of Social Work and Sociology, College Place, Washington campus \nClassification: Exempt (Salary) \nCompensation and \nBenefits: \nSalary range: $65,048 to $86,280, commensurate with teaching experience and education. \nFull-time benefits may include medical, retirement, paid time off, and more. To learn more, visit: \nwallawalla.edu/benefits. \n \nAvailable: September 1, 2026 \nDescription: Walla Walla University’s Wilma Hepker School of Social Work and Sociology seeks applications \nfor a teaching position in the College Place programs. Expertise is needed in the following areas: \nteaching, research, and social work practice. \nQualifications: • An MSW degree, with at least two years post-MSW experience in social work practice \nstrongly desired. \n• An earned doctorate in social work or a related degree is preferred.   \n• Evidence of teaching ability at the graduate level is preferred. \n• A demonstration of commitment to research, scholarly publications and \ncollegiality/teamwork is required.  \n• Active clinical social work license desired. \nApply: Prospective candidates interested in the position are asked to complete an online faculty employment \napplication and attach a cover letter, CV, and statement of teaching philosophy. Consideration of \napplicants will continue until the position is filled.  \n \nQuestions: Contact Dr. Jim Boyd, Dean, at Jim.Boyd@wallawalla.edu or 509-527-2367. Visit the School of \nSocial Work and Sociology website to learn more about the programs at \nhttps://www.wallawalla.edu/academics/areas-of-study/school-of-social-work-and-sociology/   \n \n \n"
    },
    "https://www.wallawalla.edu/fileadmin/user_upload/Academic_Administration/Job_Postings/2025-07-28_Clinical_Instructor_in_Nursing_Job_Posting.pdf": {
      "title": "Part-time Clinical Instructor",
      "description": "Part-time Clinical Instructor.   \nJob Title: Clinical Instructor Position in Nursing \n \nDepartment/School: School of Nursing, Portland, Oregon Campus  \n \nClassification: Hourly Contract Employee \n \nCompensation and \nBenefits: \nCompensation: $56 per hour for approximately 100-200 hours per quarter. No benefits other \nthan mileage for student supervision trips. \n \nAvailable: Ongoing \n \nDescription: \n \nWalla Walla University’s School of Nursing is seeking qualified candidates for a part-time \nClinical Instructor position. This role focuses on supervising and evaluating nursing students \nin clinical settings to ensure the development of professional skills and competencies. The \nideal candidate will be committed to promoting excellence in nursing education and student \nsuccess. \n \nResponsibilities: \n \n• Supervise and evaluate students’ performance in clinical settings, ensuring compliance \nwith safety, legal, and ethical standards. \n• Provide instruction, demonstration, and hands-on training in clinical techniques and \nprocedures as needed. \n• Assess and document students’ clinical progress and provide timely feedback. \n• Maintain accurate records of student attendance, evaluations, and performance. \n• Collaborate with clinical site staff to ensure effective learning experiences for students. \n• Participate in ongoing nursing education focused professional development. \n• Collaborate with colleagues to foster a positive learning environment and address diverse \nlearning needs. \n \nQualifications: \n \nEducation: \n• Master’s degree in nursing (MSN) preferred. \n \nExperience: \n• Clinical expertise and experience relevant to assigned teaching areas. \n \nLicensure: \n• Current, unencumbered RN license in WA and OR (or be eligible for). \n \n\nSkills and Abilities: \n• Strong commitment to teaching excellence and student-centered learning. \n• Strong communication and interpersonal skills.  \n• Ability to work effectively as part of a collaborative academic team. \n• Ability to work effectively with students of diverse backgrounds and learning styles. \n• Capacity to work with students one-on-one and in small groups to support individualized \nlearning. \n• Highly organized and adaptable, with the flexibility to respond to changes within the \nhealth care and academic system. \n• Must have a valid driver’s license, reliable transportation, and the ability to travel for \nstudent visits. \n \nApply: Qualified candidates interested in the position are asked to submit an online faculty \napplication and attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and statement of teaching philosophy. \n \nQuestions: Kari Firestone, School of Nursing Dean, at 509-527-2145 or kari.firestone@wallawalla.edu. \nTo learn more about our program visit our website at:  \nhttps://www.wallawalla.edu/academics/areas-of-study/nursing/ \n \n "
    },
    "https://www.wallawalla.edu/fileadmin/user_upload/Academic_Administration/Job_Postings/2026-08-19_Clinical_Instructor_in_Nursing_CP_job_posting.pdf": {
      "title": "Part-time Clinical Instructor,",
      "description": "Part-time Clinical Instructor,.   \nJob Title: Clinical Instructor Position in Nursing \n \nDepartment/School: School of Nursing, College Place, Washington campus  \n \nClassification: Hourly Contract Employee \n \nCompensation and \nBenefits: \nCompensation: $56 per hour for approximately 100-200 hours per quarter. No benefits other \nthan mileage for student supervision trips. \n \nAvailable: Ongoing \n \nDescription: \n \nWalla Walla University’s School of Nursing is seeking qualified candidates for a part-time \nClinical Instructor position. This role focuses on supervising and evaluating nursing students \nin clinical settings to ensure the development of professional skills and competencies. The \nideal candidate will be committed to promoting excellence in nursing education and student \nsuccess. \n \nResponsibilities: \n \n• Supervise and evaluate students’ performance in clinical settings, ensuring compliance \nwith safety, legal, and ethical standards. \n• Provide instruction, demonstration, and hands-on training in clinical techniques and \nprocedures as needed. \n• Assess and document students’ clinical progress and provide timely feedback. \n• Maintain accurate records of student attendance, evaluations, and performance. \n• Collaborate with clinical site staff to ensure effective learning experiences for students. \n• Participate in ongoing nursing education focused professional development. \n• Collaborate with colleagues to foster a positive learning environment and address diverse \nlearning needs. \n \nQualifications: \n \nEducation: \n• Master’s degree in nursing (MSN) preferred. \n \nExperience: \n• Clinical expertise and experience relevant to assigned teaching areas. \n \nLicensure: \n• Current, unencumbered RN license in WA and OR (or be eligible for). \n \n\nSkills and Abilities: \n• Strong commitment to teaching excellence and student-centered learning. \n• Strong communication and interpersonal skills.  \n• Ability to work effectively as part of a collaborative academic team. \n• Ability to work effectively with students of diverse backgrounds and learning styles. \n• Capacity to work with students one-on-one and in small groups to support individualized \nlearning. \n• Highly organized and adaptable, with the flexibility to respond to changes within the \nhealth care and academic system. \n• Must have a valid driver’s license, reliable transportation, and the ability to travel for \nstudent visits. \n \nApply: Qualified candidates interested in the position are asked to submit an online faculty \napplication and attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and statement of teaching philosophy. \n \nQuestions: Kari Firestone, School of Nursing Dean, at 509-527-2145 or kari.firestone@wallawalla.edu. \nTo learn more about our program visit our website at:  \nhttps://www.wallawalla.edu/academics/areas-of-study/nursing/ \n \n "
    },
    "https://www.wallawalla.edu/fileadmin/user_upload/Academic_Administration/Job_Postings/2026-10-30_Business_Faculty_job_posting.pdf": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty.  \nJob Title \n \nFull-time Faculty in Business \nDepartment/School \n \nSchool of Business \nClassification \n \nExempt (Salary) \nCompensation and \nBenefits \nPlacement of  the new hire within the salary pay grade is dependent on qualifications and \nprofessional teaching experience. The pay grade assigned to this position ranges from $67,067 \n– $86,279 annually. \nBenefits: May include medical, retirement, paid time off, and more. To learn more, visit: \nwallawalla.edu/benefits. \n \nAvailable \n \nJanuary 1, 2027 \nDescription: \n \n \nThe School of Business invites applications for a full-time faculty position in business to begin \nJanuary 1, 2027 or after.  Core teaching responsibilities in management, marketing, and strategy \nbut candidates with a range of experience including in AI/information systems, organizational \nbehavior, healthcare leadership, and entrepreneurship are also encouraged to apply. \n \nResponsibilities include: (a) teaching, academic advising, and mentoring students; (b) engaging in \nscholarly and professional activities; (c) serving on universities committees; (d) and \ndemonstrating commitment to community service.   \n \nQualifications: Preferred qualifications include: (1) earned doctorate in business/management area; (2) other \nnon-business doctorate, including juris doctorate, and an MBA degree or significant teaching and \nwork experience in the teaching area; (3) or an MBA or relevant master’s degree and significant \nteaching and work experience in the teaching area. Applicants must already have authorization to \nwork in the U.S. \n \nApplicants should be able to: (a) use technology effectively in teaching and learning; (b) bring \nreal-world experiences to the classroom; (c) work collaboratively; (d) show evidence of scholarly \nand professional activity; (e) demonstrate a commitment to Christian higher education and the \nintegration of faith and learning. \n \nApply: \n \nProspective candidates interested in the position are asked to complete an online faculty \nemployment application and attach a cover letter, CV, and statement of teaching philosophy. \nApplication materials due before December 1, 2026. Consideration of applicants will continue \nuntil the position is filled.  \n \nQuestions: For further information, please contact David Lennox by phone (509) 527-2051 or email \nDavid.Lennox@wallawalla.edu. To learn more about our program visit our website at \nhttp://business.wallawalla.edu. \n \n \n"
